1. d4 d5 2. c4 e5 {A modern defence, not found in Freeborough and Ranken's 'Chess Openings,' but analysed by Mortimer in his 'New-Century Chess-Book' in favour of Black.} 3. dxe5 d4 4. Bd2 (4. e4 {Mortimer [in his 'New Century Chess Book' according to the annotator]}) 4... Nc6 5. Nf3 Bc5 6. a3 a5 7. Bf4 Bg4 8. Nbd2 f6 9. Ne4 Be7 10. exf6 $2 (10. h3 Bf5 11. Ng3 $16) 10... Nxf6 $11 11. Qc2 $6 O-O 12. Nxf6+ $6 Bxf6 13. Bd2 $2 (13. O-O-O $5) 13... Qe7 $17 14. h3 Bh5 15. g4 Bg6 $19 16. Qd1 d3 17. e3 Bxb2 18. Bg2 Bxa1 19. Qxa1 Be4 20. Qd1 Qf7 {Source: Kent & Sussex Courier, 23 July 1902} 0-1

